637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (The Smart Expense Splitter and Group Budget Management System has been developed to address these challenges by combining expense tracking with intelligent budget management. The system allows users to create groups, record expenses, define customized sharing percentages, and monitor individual contributions in real time. It ensures transparency by maintaining a complete history of transactions and providing clear visibility into the financial status of each group member. This helps reduce misunderstandings and promotes accountability among participants.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (Financial planning and budgeting are important aspects of personal and group financial management. However, many individuals fail to track their spending patterns effectively, resulting in budget overruns and financial stress. Traditional expense management systems provide limited support for forecasting future expenses or identifying abnormal spending behavior. As a result, users often realize they have exceeded their budget only after the money has already been spent. There is therefore a growing demand for intelligent systems that can not only track expenses but also provide predictive insights and proactive financial guidance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (The rapid growth of cashless transactions and online payment systems has increased the volume and frequency of shared financial activities. As groups become larger and transactions become more complex, maintaining accurate expense records becomes increasingly difficult. Existing expense-sharing applications provide basic functionalities such as expense entry and balance calculation, but they often focus only on recording transactions rather than helping users manage their overall financial health. Users still need to manually analyze spending habits, monitor budgets, and determine how to avoid overspending.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (A key feature of the proposed system is its ability to analyze spending patterns using historical transaction data. By studying users' spending behavior, the system can identify trends, estimate future expenses, and generate predictive budget alerts before a budget limit is exceeded. These insights help users make informed financial decisions and encourage responsible spending habits. Additionally, the system can detect unusual or unexpected expenses and notify users, allowing them to take corrective actions at an early stage.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (In today's digital world, managing shared expenses has become an essential part of everyday life. Whether it is a group of friends planning a trip, roommates sharing rent and utility bills, students organizing events, families managing household expenses, or teams working on projects, people frequently need to divide costs among multiple members. Although digital payment platforms have simplified money transfers, tracking who paid what and ensuring fair cost distribution remains a significant challenge. Manual calculations, handwritten records, and spreadsheets often lead to confusion, calculation errors, forgotten payments, and disputes among group members.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
