666 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 400 0 R
/T (Another significant challenge lies in the settlement of debts among multiple users. In groups with numerous transactions, determining the most efficient way to settle balances can become complex. Existing systems may require multiple transactions between members, increasing inconvenience and reducing efficiency. Furthermore, many applications do not offer personalized financial insights that could assist users in making informed spending decisions.)
/E (Another significant challenge lies in the settlement of debts among multiple users. In groups with numerous transactions, determining the most efficient way to settle balances can become complex. Existing systems may require multiple transactions between members, increasing inconvenience and reducing efficiency. Furthermore, many applications do not offer personalized financial insights that could assist users in making informed spending decisions.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 400 0 R
/T (From a technical standpoint, there is a significant challenge in integrating expense tracking, budget management, spending analytics, and debt settlement into a single unified platform. While many applications provide basic expense recording and balance calculation features, they often operate independently without offering intelligent financial insights. Users must manually monitor budgets, analyze spending patterns, and determine efficient settlement methods, which can be time-consuming and error-prone. Moreover, most existing systems lack predictive capabilities to identify potential budget overruns or unusual spending behavior in real time. This absence of automation and financial intelligence reduces efficiency and limits users' ability to make informed financial decisions, highlighting the need for a comprehensive and intelligent expense management solution.)
/E (From a technical standpoint, there is a significant challenge in integrating expense tracking, budget management, spending analytics, and debt settlement into a single unified platform. While many applications provide basic expense recording and balance calculation features, they often operate independently without offering intelligent financial insights. Users must manually monitor budgets, analyze spending patterns, and determine efficient settlement methods, which can be time-consuming and error-prone. Moreover, most existing systems lack predictive capabilities to identify potential budget overruns or unusual spending behavior in real time. This absence of automation and financial intelligence reduces efficiency and limits users' ability to make informed financial decisions, highlighting the need for a comprehensive and intelligent expense management solution.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
