/E (Another important objective is to automate the process of calculating and splitting expenses among group members. In many group situations, expenses may not always be divided equally because different members may contribute different amounts or may be responsible for different portions of an expense. Therefore, the proposed system should support flexible expense-sharing mechanisms such as equal splitting, percentage-based splitting, and customized contribution rules. The system automatically calculates the amount payable by each member based on the selected sharing method. This reduces the possibility of human errors in calculations and ensures that the distribution of expenses remains accurate and consistent.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
709 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 404 0 R
/E (The project also aims to provide effective group and category-based budget management. Users should be able to define a budget for a particular group and, where necessary, allocate separate limits to categories of expenses. The system should continuously compare recorded expenses with the allocated budget and update the remaining amount as new transactions are entered. This allows users to monitor their financial position throughout the duration of a group activity. By providing clear information about total spending, budget utilization, and remaining budget, the system encourages users to maintain better control over their financial activities and reduces the possibility of unexpected overspending.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
