/E (The proposed system additionally aims to introduce intelligent spending analysis by using available historical expense information. Traditional expense-splitting applications generally focus on recording transactions and calculating balances, but they provide limited support for understanding spending behavior. The proposed system extends these capabilities by analyzing recorded expenses to identify spending patterns, commonly used categories, unusual expenses, and rapidly increasing expenditure. Such analysis can help users understand how their group budget is being utilized and identify areas where spending may require additional attention. The objective is to convert stored transaction information into meaningful financial insights that can support better awareness and planning.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
