/E (A minimum of 8 GB of RAM is essential for the development environment, while 16 GB is recommended for smoother performance when running multiple development tools, database services, browsers, and testing environments concurrently. Since modern web applications may require several frameworks, libraries, dependencies, and development servers to operate simultaneously, sufficient memory helps reduce system slowdowns. A solid-state drive \(SSD\) is also preferable to a traditional hard disk because of its faster read and write speeds, resulting in quicker application startup, dependency installation, database operations, and file access.)
