>>
endobj
1627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 454 0 R
/E (To evaluate the performance, accuracy, and reliability of the Smart Expense Splitter and Group Budget Management System, comprehensive testing was conducted across all major modules and functionalities. The objective of testing was to verify that each feature operated according to the specified requirements and that all system components interacted correctly without errors. Various test cases were designed to validate group creation, member management, expense recording, expense splitting, budget monitoring, analytics generation, debt settlement calculations, API communication, database operations, and user interface responsiveness. During testing, different input scenarios were executed, including both valid and invalid data, to examine system behavior under various conditions.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 454 0 R
/T (The Group Management Module was tested by creating new groups, updating group details, retrieving group information, and deleting groups. The system successfully stored and displayed group information while maintaining data consistency within the PostgreSQL database. The Member Management Module was tested by adding, updating, viewing, and removing members from groups. All member records were accurately maintained and linked to their corresponding groups through foreign key relationships. Expense Management testing involved recording expenses with different categories, amounts, dates, and payer details. The application successfully stored expense records and associated split information while maintaining transaction integrity.)
/E (The Group Management Module was tested by creating new groups, updating group details, retrieving group information, and deleting groups. The system successfully stored and displayed group information while maintaining data consistency within the PostgreSQL database. The Member Management Module was tested by adding, updating, viewing, and removing members from groups. All member records were accurately maintained and linked to their corresponding groups through foreign key relationships. Expense Management testing involved recording expenses with different categories, amounts, dates, and payer details. The application successfully stored expense records and associated split information while maintaining transaction integrity.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 454 0 R
/T (The Expense Splitting Module was tested using equal split, percentage-based split, and custom split methods. The system accurately calculated individual contributions and validated whether percentages totaled 100% or custom contributions matched the total expense amount. Budget Management testing verified that the application correctly monitored spending against predefined budgets, updated remaining balances automatically, and calculated budget utilization percentages whenever new expenses were recorded. The dashboard consistently reflected updated budget statistics in real time.)
/E (The Expense Splitting Module was tested using equal split, percentage-based split, and custom split methods. The system accurately calculated individual contributions and validated whether percentages totaled 100% or custom contributions matched the total expense amount. Budget Management testing verified that the application correctly monitored spending against predefined budgets, updated remaining balances automatically, and calculated budget utilization percentages whenever new expenses were recorded. The dashboard consistently reflected updated budget statistics in real time.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1630 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 454 0 R
/T (The Analytics Module was tested using various expense datasets to generate spending summaries, category-wise expenditure reports, contribution statistics, and financial trends. All generated reports were accurate and matched the corresponding database records. Interactive charts created using Chart.js successfully visualized financial information through pie charts, bar graphs, and line charts, allowing users to interpret spending patterns more effectively. The Debt Settlement Module was tested with multiple expense-sharing scenarios involving different contributors and participants. The system correctly identified creditors and debtors, calculated net balances, and generated optimized settlement recommendations that minimized the number of transactions required for repayment.)
/E (The Analytics Module was tested using various expense datasets to generate spending summaries, category-wise expenditure reports, contribution statistics, and financial trends. All generated reports were accurate and matched the corresponding database records. Interactive charts created using Chart.js successfully visualized financial information through pie charts, bar graphs, and line charts, allowing users to interpret spending patterns more effectively. The Debt Settlement Module was tested with multiple expense-sharing scenarios involving different contributors and participants. The system correctly identified creditors and debtors, calculated net balances, and generated optimized settlement recommendations that minimized the number of transactions required for repayment.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1631 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 454 0 R
/T (API testing was performed using Postman to validate all REST endpoints implemented in the Node.js and Express.js backend. CRUD operations for groups, members, expenses, budgets, and analytics were tested extensively. All API endpoints returned appropriate HTTP status codes and JSON responses. Database testing confirmed that records were inserted, updated, retrieved, and deleted correctly within PostgreSQL. Foreign key constraints, primary keys, transactions, and integrity rules functioned as expected, ensuring data consistency and reliability.)
/E (API testing was performed using Postman to validate all REST endpoints implemented in the Node.js and Express.js backend. CRUD operations for groups, members, expenses, budgets, and analytics were tested extensively. All API endpoints returned appropriate HTTP status codes and JSON responses. Database testing confirmed that records were inserted, updated, retrieved, and deleted correctly within PostgreSQL. Foreign key constraints, primary keys, transactions, and integrity rules functioned as expected, ensuring data consistency and reliability.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [7]
>>
