/P 471 0 R
/E (The Smart Expense Splitter and Group Budget Management System is a web-based financial management application developed to simplify the process of tracking shared expenses, managing group budgets, analyzing spending patterns, and settling financial balances among multiple users. The project was designed to address the common challenges faced by friends, families, roommates, students, and project teams when managing collective expenses. Traditional methods of expense tracking often involve manual calculations, spreadsheets, and informal record-keeping, which can lead to errors, misunderstandings, and inefficient financial management. The proposed system provides a centralized platform that automates these activities and ensures transparency among all participants.)
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1791 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 471 0 R
/T (The application was developed using a modern three-tier architecture consisting of a frontend, backend, and database layer. The frontend was built using HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and Chart.js to provide an interactive and user-friendly interface. The backend was implemented using Node.js and Express.js, which handle business logic, request processing, validation, and communication with the database. PostgreSQL was used as the relational database management system to store group information, member details, expense records, budget data, and settlement information securely and efficiently.)
/E (The application was developed using a modern three-tier architecture consisting of a frontend, backend, and database layer. The frontend was built using HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and Chart.js to provide an interactive and user-friendly interface. The backend was implemented using Node.js and Express.js, which handle business logic, request processing, validation, and communication with the database. PostgreSQL was used as the relational database management system to store group information, member details, expense records, budget data, and settlement information securely and efficiently.)
/Pg 91 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
