1949 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (To set up the Smart Expense Splitter and Group Budget Management System, the required software must first be installed. This includes Node.js for running the backend server, PostgreSQL for database management, and Visual Studio Code as the development environment. On macOS, PostgreSQL can be installed using Homebrew. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1950 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (These tools provide the foundation for developing, running, and testing the application.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1951 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (After installing the required software, the project files are downloaded from the GitHub repository and opened in Visual Studio Code. The project dependencies are then installed using npm, Node.js's package manager. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1952 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (This process automatically downloads and configures all required libraries, including Express for backend development, pg for PostgreSQL connectivity, and dotenv for managing environment variables.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1953 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (Next, a PostgreSQL database is created and the schema file is executed. The schema creates the application's tables, namely expense_groups, members, expenses, and expense_splits.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1954 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E ( These tables store information about groups, group members, expenses, and expense-sharing details. Relationships between the tables are maintained using primary keys and foreign keys to ensure data integrity.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1955 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (The database connection settings are then configured in a .env file. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1956 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (This file securely stores information such as the database host, port number, database name, username, and password. Using environment variables helps keep sensitive information separate from the application code and improves security.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1957 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (Once the database configuration is complete, the backend server is started using Node.js. The Express server establishes a connection with PostgreSQL and exposes REST API endpoints that allow the frontend to perform operations such as creating groups, adding members, recording expenses, and retrieving analytics data.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1958 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (Finally, the frontend is launched in a web browser. The user can access the dashboard, create groups, add expenses, view budget analytics, and monitor settlements. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1959 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 482 0 R
/E (Successful setup is verified by ensuring that data can be stored in PostgreSQL, retrieved through the API, and displayed correctly on the user interface along with charts and analytical insights.)
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
